# Steam Input injects chord keyboard presses via XTEST inside XWayland, so
# Hyprland binds never see them - only X clients can. This catches the media
# keys from controller chords (PS+stick etc.) and routes them to wpctl.
# Physical media keys are consumed by Hyprland's own binds before XWayland, so
# these fire for the injected ones only. 5% steps: chords are taps, not holds,
# unlike the repeating 1% keyboard binds.

"wpctl set-volume -l 1 @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 5%+"
    XF86AudioRaiseVolume

"wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 5%-"
    XF86AudioLowerVolume

"wpctl set-mute @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ toggle"
    XF86AudioMute
